{"type":"text","timestamp":1772832208874,"sessionID":"ses_33af8db55ffe2TXh62DSc9CwFB","part":{"id":"prt_cc50880d7001GtNDkuV3iU2Afn","sessionID":"ses_33af8db55ffe2TXh62DSc9CwFB","messageID":"msg_cc5085ed6001kohe9YoYuPQZTD","type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the codebase, I found that:\n\n1. **The API key is stored via environment variable** `SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY` (or falls back to no auth if not set)\n2. **The frontend already has a key modal** implemented in `server/templates/index.html`\n3. **localStorage is already used** (`mad_key`) for key persistence\n4. **However**, the current implementation sends all data to the frontend and hides it with CSS when unauthenticated - this doesn't meet the requirement that \"backend should not send any actual data\"\n\nThe main missing pieces are:\n- Backend should NOT send data when unauthenticated (currently sends full page, just hidden)\n- Logout button needed (as confirmed)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"plan\": \"## Feature Implementation Plan: WebUI Key Prompt Authentication\\n\\n### Overview\\nImplement a modal-based authentication system for the MAD dashboard webui. The backend already has `SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY` environment variable support, but needs modifications to not send content data when unauthenticated.\\n\\n### Backend Changes (server/)\\n\\n1. **Modify api.go** - When dashboard key is required and not authenticated:\\n   - Serve a minimal \\\"locked\\\" page instead of the full dashboard\\n   - The locked page should only contain the key modal (no client data, no feature data)\\n   - This ensures \\\"backend should not send any actual data\\\" requirement is met\\n\\n2. **Modify index.html template** - Update conditional rendering:\\n   - Remove CSS-based hiding of `#dashboard-content` \\n   - Instead, render different content based on `{{.Authenticated}}` - either show the full dashboard OR show only the key modal\\n   - Add logout button (user confirmed requirement)\\n\\n3. **Add logout functionality** in index.html:\\n   - Add a \\\"Logout\\\" or \\\"Clear Key\\\" button in the header\\n   - Function to clear `mad_key` from localStorage\\n   - Redirect to home page without key query param\\n\\n### Frontend Changes (server/templates/index.html)\\n\\n1. **Add logout button** to header area (line ~213):\\n   ```html\\n   <button onclick=\\\"logout()\\\" style=\\\"padding:0.4rem 0.8rem;background:#30363d;color:#c9d1d9;border:none;border-radius:4px;cursor:pointer;font-size:0.85rem;\\\">Logout</button>\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Add logout JavaScript function** (in script section):\\n   ```javascript\\n   function logout() {\\n       localStorage.removeItem('mad_key');\\n       window.location.href = '/';\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Update key modal** - Make sure it shows when:\\n   - No key in localStorage AND no key in URL query param\\n   - Auth fails (401 response)\\n\\n### Backend Logic Changes (api.go)\\n\\nIn the root handler (`/`), modify to serve minimal content when not authenticated:\\n- When `authenticated == false`, only render the page shell with the key modal\\n- Do NOT include any client data, feature data, or stage groups\\n- This can be done by passing empty data structures when not authenticated\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Verify modal appears on fresh load with no key\\n- Verify modal appears when invalid key is entered\\n- Verify key is saved to localStorage on valid entry\\n- Verify key persists on page reload\\n- Verify logout button clears key and shows modal\\n- Verify backend returns minimal content when unauthenticated (no sensitive data in response)\"\n}\n```","time":{"start":1772832208871,"end":1772832208871}}}
